<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοσος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 and 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνουσος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without
				sickness, healthy, sound,</i> of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκηθέες καὶ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.255
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. καὶ ἀγήραοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					143
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				33a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπηρος, ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῶστον δὲ τὸ ζῆν ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					356
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνόσως, διάγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.267
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ᾤχετ᾽ ἐς ἡμιθέους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(2).472.13
				</span></i>
			 (Megalopolis, <span class="entity">ii/iii A.D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. κακῶν</span>
			<i>untouchid by</i> ill, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				982
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πρὸς τὰ ἄλλα ἀρρωστήματα,
				τῶν ἄλλων ἀρρωστημάτων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				604a12
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of a season,
				<i>free from sickness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτος ἄ. ἐς τὰς ἄλλας ἀσθενείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.49
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕξις, λόγος ἄ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.7b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>not causing disease, harmless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1201
			</span></i>.</div>
